    "done_when": "Shared interface between the mesh and the tree (both nodes build to it): the mesh returns a frozen dataclass ContourMesh in nova/equilibrium/contour_tree_mesh.py with fixed-capacity jax arrays vertex_rz (V,2) m, vertex_psi (V,) Wb, vertex_valid (V,) bool, vertex_is_wall (V,) bool, edges (E,2) int32 vertex indices, edge_valid (E,) bool, triangles (T,3) int32, triangle_valid (T,) bool, plus the capacities V, E, T and an overflow flag; the tree consumes vertex_psi, vertex_valid, vertex_is_wall, edges and edge_valid only, and sigma from contour_tree.sigma_for_state. In nova/equilibrium/contour_tree.py (the section 1 contract already lives there; read it and the plan's sections 1, 2 and 4 at main), add a jit- and vmap-traceable function that takes vertex values, validity and wall masks, an edge list and sigma, and returns the contour tree into ContourTreeResult's node and edge arrays with critical_type 0, 1 or 2 on raw psi. It computes the join tree of sigma*psi (superlevel sets descending from the maximum) and the split tree, then merges them. Ties break by simulation of simplicity (vertex index as the secondary key), so no two values are equal. Every wall vertex is connected to one virtual outside node valued below every interior level, so a region meets the wall where it joins the outside node, at its highest wall vertex. Node and edge capacities come from ContourTreeResult, and an overflow sets a named receipt flag rather than truncating. Port the semantics of /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-efit/src/EFIT/contour_tree.f90 and its Python oracle (see docs/evidence/contour-tree-topology-authority/reuse-map.md rows 4 to 6); reuse the fixed-slot connectivity kernels named there. tests/test_contour_tree_merge.py, on synthetic piecewise-linear fields over small triangulated grids (a single maximum; two maxima joined by a saddle; a plateau needing tie breaking; a field touching a wall), asserts: the node set and critical types match the analytic critical points; node count minus edge count is 1; each saddle's level equals the level where a brute-force connected-component count of the superlevel set over the edge graph changes; the batched (vmap) and per-field trees are identical; an over-capacity field reports the overflow flag. Negative control: disable the tie breaking and the plateau test fails, logged. Fresh process, in place on the fleet allocation (TMPDIR=/tmp, JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, configure_dtypes before any array), gates in the foreground. Logs under docs/figures/contour-tree-topology-authority/tree/ (force-add; *.log is gitignored). Do not edit any other nova module.",
